# Reasoning agent — environment template
#
# LOCAL DEV (`agentcore dev`): copy this file to `.env` and fill in values.
#     cp .env.example .env
# DEPLOYED (`agentcore deploy`): do NOT set these here. The gateway URL is
#   auto-injected into the runtime when the gateway is bound to it (README
#   "Wire the gateway + targets" step); AWS region/credentials come from the
#   runtime's execution role.
#
# `.env` is gitignored; this `.env.example` is the committed template.

# ── AGENTCORE_GATEWAY_CRYLOCANVASGW_URL ──────────────────────────────────────
# MCP Gateway endpoint. The Reasoning agent connects here for the Pricing / CFN
# / Docs tools. The variable name is fixed by the gateway name (CryloCanvasGw):
# AGENTCORE_GATEWAY_<GATEWAYNAME_UPPERCASE>_URL.
#
#   - Leave UNSET to run with NO MCP tools — the local-dev guard no-ops the
#     client, so you can test the model + the two local @tools without a gateway.
#   - To exercise the real tools locally, paste the URL printed after the
#     gateway is deployed. Format:
#     https://<gateway-id>.gateway.bedrock-agentcore.<region>.amazonaws.com/mcp
AGENTCORE_GATEWAY_CRYLOCANVASGW_URL=

# ── AWS_REGION ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Region used for the Bedrock model call (Claude Sonnet 4.5). Must be a region
# where you've enabled Bedrock model access. Only needed for local dev — the
# deployed runtime uses its own region. AWS credentials come from your usual
# AWS CLI config / profile, never from this file.
AWS_REGION=ap-south-1
